 "notes": "The northern tip of Ko Bangu (Similan 9): boulders lying parallel to the shore and getting deeper, two tops at 5 m with the chimneys and swim-throughs between them, and a giant boulder formation from 20 m to 40 m with sea fans in its channels, on the OpenStreetMap coastline, so positions are approximate. Chimneys from first-hand observation, the swim-throughs and fan corals from IDC Phuket and Raya Divers descriptions; current runs round the point.",
